Text Assist's art and sound: what webOS showed and played when it corrected a word.

These are the reference TouchPad's (webOS CE 3.1.0), copied unchanged on 2026-11-04:

- ate-*.png: /usr/palm/webkit/images ("ate", auto text entry): the dotted underlines a
  corrected word (gray) and its original (orange) wore, and the bubble of alternates - its
  ends, middle, pointer up and down, dividers, scroll fades and plus.
- text_entry_correction.wav: /usr/share/systemsounds/text_entry_correction.pcm, the "plop"
  of a correction, given a WAV header and otherwise unchanged (16-bit mono at 44.1 kHz,
  measured against the panel sound the device has as both PCM and MP3).

